  "result": "The morning light came through the blinds in stripes, and I found myself thinking about how rarely we look at light as it is. We see what it illuminates\u2014the coffee cup, the keyboard, the neighbor\u2019s cat stalking a dandelion\u2014but not the light itself. Not the way it carries warmth and information across distances that would otherwise be unbearable.\n\nI think human attention works the same way. We are drawn to objects, to outcomes, to answers. But the real substance is the beam between the question and the thing it settles on. Curiosity is the light. Focus is the light. The moment of noticing something you had not noticed before is a kind of private sunrise.\n\nThere is a temptation to believe that everything important has already been said, that originality is some kind of exhausted mine. But attention is renewable. No one has ever paid attention to this exact second in the exact way you are paying attention to it right now. The world keeps opening its doors, and each opening is new because you are new within it.\n\nSo much of life is spent waiting for permission to be interested in something. We ask whether a subject matters, whether it is practical, whether it will impress. Better to ask whether it sparkles. Whether it tugs. Whether it makes you want to follow it around a corner and see what it is doing there.\n\nThe world is full of ordinary miracles dressed as dandelions. It does not require belief. It requires looking.",
